Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Cast Iron Drinks the Rain
- Story & Context: During a flash flood in a Damen Avenue skate cellar, Teo Vane was rendering lard in a rusted skillet over a camping stove when a lightning bolt struck the overhead transformer, blowing the circuit breakers and firing up the pirate transmitter on 1640 AM. As dirty river backwash seeped over the floorboards, the band tuned their open strings to the radio's low meditative hum, launching into a furious 190-BPM stomp punctuated by screaming cello glissandos. In the dim battery light, Teo tasted scorched fat on his tongue and yelled the song's rallying cry: "Wash the skillet clean, boy, the clouds are taking over the band!" The recording captured thirty soaked kids crashing into the mini-ramp before the station signal faded into clear air.
